<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  dev.wingmen.commitment-sweeper — CAI-RESP-1029 build 1/2. Fires durable commitments
  (held_commitments, migration 051) whose clock has come due.

  AUTHORED + LOADED + OWNED by orch-console (Nazim). This is the trigger whose EXISTENCE
  CAI-RESP-1029 makes a precondition: no build lane may become ephemeral until its spawn
  trigger has been built, loaded, and EXERCISED.

  PATHS VERIFIED FOR THIS HOST (Sheikhs-Mini, user sheikhmusa) 2026-08-17 03:36Z. Only
  /Users/sheikhmusa exists here. The residency_sweep precedent hardcoded /Users/Musa — a path
  that does not exist on this machine — so that job could not have run even if it had been
  loaded, and it has now been dead six weeks. IF YOU LOAD THIS FROM A DIFFERENT HOST,
  RE-VERIFY EVERY PATH FIRST. That is the failure mode, not the SQL.

  WHY StartInterval AND NOT StartCalendarInterval: a commitment's whole value is being fired
  NEAR its due time. A daily calendar job would make every deadline up to 24h late, which is
  indistinguishable from the failure this replaces. 300s is a compromise between promptness
  and noise; the sweeper is idempotent, so a tick with nothing due costs one cheap query.

  ⚠ RunAtLoad is TRUE deliberately: an unexercised trigger is not a trigger. Loading it fires
  it once immediately, so "it is loaded" and "it has run" are established in the same act
  rather than left as an assumption someone has to check later.

  ⚠ THE DEFECT THIS RUNNER ALREADY AVOIDS: launchd inherits NOTHING. A3's runner read
  os.environ only and never called load_dotenv, so it worked by hand (our shells descend from
  a claude process with .env sourced) and failed under the scheduler on its very first real
  fire. commitment_sweeper.py calls load_dotenv(ROOT/'.env') at import for exactly that
  reason. Do NOT "fix" a future MISSING-DSN by putting a DSN in this plist: this file is 0644,
  .env is 0600, and moving a credential into a world-readable file to satisfy a scheduler is a
  real regression.
-->
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>dev.wingmen.commitment-sweeper</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key><array>
    <string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/.venv/bin/python3</string>
    <string>-m</string>
    <string>nervous_system.commitment_sweeper</string>
    <string>--fire</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>300</integer>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key><dict>
    <key>HOME</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa</string>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/logs/commitment-sweeper.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/sheikhmusa/wingmen/orchestrator/logs/commitment-sweeper.out.log</string>
</dict></plist>
